WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
- So when I first saw your book,

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.792
I had one word, I was like damn!

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:05.780
(audience laughing)

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.613
Get it!

00:00:06.613 --> 00:00:09.140
Like I can't hang with you anymore!

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.809
Come on, like you are so fit.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:14.200
I'm gonna put this by my treadmill

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.000
in hopes that it will motivate me.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.020
- Well, I don't know about that,

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.020
you know everybody's got
their own journey for sure.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.706
- Oh my gosh.
- And for me, you know,

00:00:20.706 --> 00:00:22.830
the only reason we wrote the book was,

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.730
usually you get five or 10 minutes

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.440
when you're doing interviews, as you know.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.950
And it's usually about
where you're touring,

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.308
when's your tour start,
when's your album coming out,

00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:32.100
what's your next single.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.160
- It's not necessarily in depth.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.250
- How are the kids and all that.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.064
Oh,, by the way you got in
shape, how'd you do that?

00:00:36.064 --> 00:00:37.730
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And we got two minutes,

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.400
and you never have time to
really say all of what it does.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.280
And it's really, as much physical,

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.003
it was mental for me in a lot of ways.

00:00:44.003 --> 00:00:45.613
(audience cheering)

00:00:45.613 --> 00:00:47.990
- I mean, yeah, that's just a few photos

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.250
from the book of life.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.760
- It's painted, it's all photoshopped.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.344
- That ain't painted,
you worked hard for that.

00:00:54.344 --> 00:00:55.610
What inspired you to get in shape?

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.424
- Well, I had been an
athlete my entire life.

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.257
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:00:59.900
- And I come from a long line of athletes.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.040
My dad was a professional baseball player,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.010
my uncle was a professional
baseball player,

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.190
so I have some athletic DNA in me.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.904
And I was an athlete my
whole life growing up

00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:10.270
and I kinda let that get away from me.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.250
You know, being on the road

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.680
and being part of that lifestyle

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.384
and not taking care of yourself.

00:01:15.384 --> 00:01:16.217
- And like going from
one place to the next,

00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:17.250
it's hard to like eat healthy.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.766
- Yeah, it's hard.

00:01:18.766 --> 00:01:19.599
- It's a lot harder.

00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:20.432
- It's tougher, but you just have to

00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:21.750
dig a little deeper and find it.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.904
But you know I was going
through a tough time in my life,

00:01:24.904 --> 00:01:27.510
I lost my dad, who I was
just getting to know.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.370
My dad died at 59 of brain cancer,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.440
and I didn't know him growing up,

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.120
so I was just getting to know him.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.740
And then my stepdad passed
away during that time,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.213
and my grandparents, and my coach

00:01:37.213 --> 00:01:39.497
who was a real mentor to me.
- That's a lot of loss.

00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:42.500
- So it was a lot of loss, but you know,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.470
a lot of times we fall back

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.200
and use things as excuses as well too.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.780
And I was going through a
thing with my record label.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.270
So, everything is relative to everybody,

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.630
you know, no matter what
station of life you're at,

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.050
or how much money you make or don't make

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.570
or whatever job you have,

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.210
everybody has issues to deal with,

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.680
and you gotta find a
way to deal with them.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.170
And I was dealing with them the wrong way.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.504
And my wife told me I needed
to get my stuff together,

00:02:03.504 --> 00:02:05.170
- Yeah.
- And then I was at a movie-

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.003
- Did she say stuff?

00:02:06.003 --> 00:02:08.170
(Audience laugher)

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.099
I know she's a Mississippi
girl, she did not say stuff.

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:11.050
- She's a Mississippi girl,

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.230
she can be quite colorful
with the English language.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.063
- Yes me too.

00:02:15.063 --> 00:02:18.300
- Absolutely, but then we were at a movie.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.050
We took the kids to see
a movie, a holiday movie,

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.050
and this was, I guess, 10 or 11 years -

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.050
Gracie's 22 now so she must
have been 10 or 11 years old,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:27.440
so it was a while back.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.880
I had done a movie that I sort of,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.930
wanted to sort of not think about,

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.630
and didn't think about
the trailer being on,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.340
and it wasn't that it was a bad
movie or anything like that,

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.240
I just didn't like me.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.280
But, sure enough, the first
thing that popped on the screen

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.410
was the trailer of the
movie that I was in,

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.120
and my face on a hundred-foot screen,

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.877
and my daughter Gracie
looks at me and says,

00:02:45.877 --> 00:02:47.931
"Jeez dad, you need to do something".

00:02:47.931 --> 00:02:48.764
(Audience laughter)

00:02:48.764 --> 00:02:52.211
- Dude, I'm telling you kids
are wrong, kids are wrong.

00:02:52.211 --> 00:02:55.960
- But to me, it was
funny, and she meant it,

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.230
but she meant it in a lot
of different ways I think,

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.182
because kids pay more attention

00:02:59.182 --> 00:03:00.590
to a lot of things in your life

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.320
than what you ever realize
that they pay attention to,

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.040
and she meant it in a
lot of different ways.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.050
And it was sort of a clarity call for me.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:09.330
And it wasn't overnight,
it was a gradual process,

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.150
and it was, you know, three
steps forward and two steps back

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.571
and it always is and it always will be.

00:03:14.571 --> 00:03:17.040
You're never going to arrive at a goal,

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.240
you're always working
to get to some place.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.491
But what I've found is, trying to keep up

00:03:22.491 --> 00:03:26.360
a consistent physical
practice has helped me

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.800
find other disciplines and other things.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.189
And, you know, we think of discipline as

00:03:30.189 --> 00:03:32.290
sort of this cage that
your put yourself in

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:35.030
when you decide to apply
discipline to your life.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.880
What I've discovered is discipline really

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.830
opens the door to the cage that you're in,

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.380
and it allows you to find other
things that you're good at.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.900
- Is this all in the
book? Because I'm like-

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.491
- [Tim] Well most of it's in there, yeah.

00:03:44.491 --> 00:03:46.840
- I'm just saying, I'm in, this is wow.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.673
- Well it works, you know.

00:03:47.673 --> 00:03:49.140
The stronger you build your platform,

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.500
the higher you can leap, and
that what I'm trying to do,

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.130
and that what I want
everyone to experience,

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.340
and hopefully somebody will get -

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.650
if one person gets something
out of it then right on.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.830
- I already have, I told
you, right by the treadmill.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.350
It's like, it's amazing.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.750
Okay so, how did you,

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.270
I know that you went to the physical part

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.900
and it kinda helped you
mentally and emotionally,

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.240
but how do you deal with that much loss?

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.900
Like to other people,
like because I feel like

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.950
we all experience things
to have a testimony

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:12.783
to tell other people,

00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:13.890
to get them through it as well.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.540
- Absolutely, for me, you know,

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.730
after you sort of realize the loss,

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.230
you look at what you have.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.063
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:04:21.063 --> 00:04:22.480
- I had a lot of great things in my life.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.850
I mean, I have the best wife that I could

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.290
ever imagine myself having.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.140
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.610
- And I got three great daughters.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.230
And I got a great career,

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.080
coming from a small town in Louisiana

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.240
where I grew up with nothing in my life,

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.936
except for the love of a mom.

00:04:36.936 --> 00:04:37.769
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:37.769 --> 00:04:38.910
- Without any - and my grandparents.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.700
Without that, I don't
know where I would be.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.330
So to be at that place in my life,

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.510
to have all the things I ever possibly

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.530
could dream of in my life,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.210
it made me look around and say,

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.035
you know, I got a lot
more to be thankful for

00:04:51.035 --> 00:04:53.217
than to worry about the cycle of life.

00:04:53.217 --> 00:04:55.290
- What a beautiful way
to turn that around.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.995
- Yeah, well, you know,

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:59.467
with a Mississippi boot in your ass too.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.246
(Audience laughter)

00:05:01.246 --> 00:05:02.677
- She's like look here sir.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.435
Do you work out with Faith,
does she work out with you?

00:05:05.435 --> 00:05:06.303
- She works out yeah, you know-

00:05:06.303 --> 00:05:08.170
- [Kelly] Because she
always looks so good!

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.417
- She's pretty hot.

00:05:09.417 --> 00:05:10.250
- [Kelly] I know!

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.083
(Audience laughter)

00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:11.916
- She's pretty hot.

00:05:11.916 --> 00:05:13.890
- I know.
- As the kids have grown up,

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.310
and as the kids have gotten older,

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.870
we find that we're getting to spend

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.130
a little bit more time
together in the gym downstairs,

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.820
so I'm enjoying that for sure.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.080
- [Kelly] That's so cool, all right.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.117
I also was reading your pre-interview

00:05:23.117 --> 00:05:24.713
and I didn't know that you love to cook.

00:05:24.713 --> 00:05:26.536
- [Tim] I love to cook.
- You and Faith cook, yeah.

00:05:26.536 --> 00:05:28.550
- We both cook, Faith's
a fantastic cook, I mean-

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.383
- [Kelly] Yeah I bet.

00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:30.304
- She can cook anything.

00:05:30.304 --> 00:05:31.769
- [Kelly] She does everything great too.

00:05:31.769 --> 00:05:32.602
- She does everything.

00:05:32.602 --> 00:05:33.435
- She's beautiful.

00:05:33.435 --> 00:05:34.268
(Audience laughter)

00:05:34.268 --> 00:05:35.697
- I know, she married way below

00:05:35.697 --> 00:05:37.580
- Whatever, whatever.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:38.561
- But yeah, she's a great cook.

00:05:38.561 --> 00:05:41.210
I do the staples, I mean
we cook some healthy,

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:42.330
a lot of healthy stuff,

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.438
but we cook some stuff that's
not so healthy as well.

00:05:44.438 --> 00:05:45.271
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:45.271 --> 00:05:46.819
- I mean chicken and dumplings
is a big go-to at our house.

00:05:46.819 --> 00:05:47.652
- Yeah, it's Southern.

00:05:47.652 --> 00:05:48.710
- That's sorta how I hooked Faith,

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.139
was with chicken and dumplings.

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:50.972
- What do you mean you sorta-

00:05:50.972 --> 00:05:51.840
- I took 'em to her house.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.490
We were touring together, I
didn't know her that well,

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.210
and she lived right down the road from me.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.043
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:58.043 --> 00:05:59.020
- And I made some chicken and dumplings,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.870
and I thought, you know, I'll take some

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:02.530
chicken and dumplings and some cornbread

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.270
down to Faith Hill and we'll
see how that works out.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:06.067
- I just wanna, I wanna
be a fly - it worked.

00:06:07.169 --> 00:06:08.580
I wanna be a fly on that wall.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.850
- I still cook them every now and then

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:10.770
to see if it still works.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.016
- You're like you still love me right?

00:06:13.016 --> 00:06:13.849
(Audience laughter)

